      "problem": "If $x=-2$ then $|x+3|-|3x-1|+x=$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=-2$ and then evaluate the absolute values before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+3|-|3x-1|+x & = \\\\ |-2+3|-|3(-2)-1|+(-2) & = \\\\ |1|-|-6-1|-2 & = \\\\ |1|-|-7|-2 & = \\\\ 1-7-2 & = \\\\ -8 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
